K12e — connector prerequisites hidden by an absent upstream fragment, 2026-09-28
============================================================================

The frozen connector collection has no config file. Both the historical
970-program Images and the newly reviewed build configuration disable
CONFIG_CONNECTOR; CONFIG_PROC_EVENTS is consequently absent. The unchanged
proc_filter executable fails socket(AF_NETLINK, SOCK_DGRAM, NETLINK_CONNECTOR)
with EPROTONOSUPPORT before subscribing to any process events. Its old paired
FAIL is not a compiler regression, and it is not a runtime PASS.

The source's drivers/connector/Kconfig explicitly requires CONNECTOR=y for
PROC_EVENTS. Loading a separately built cn.ko cannot supply process events.
The next separately identified configuration must enable BOTH options as
built-ins, rebuild the matching pair, then execute the unchanged original.
No live config, object, Image or receipt is changed in this diagnosis.

Shared tooling repair:
  A new configuration-audit RED found that the report only listed connector
  under missingFragments, hiding the now-known prerequisite from follow-up.
  It now reports pinned source-reviewed requirements separately from original
  fragments. Changed/missing test or Kconfig bytes yield SOURCE_CHANGED and
  no inherited conclusion. Disabled/module/built-in distinctions remain;
  results are never rewritten and other collections are not silently inferred.
  All 263 K1 Python tests, targeted Ruff and git diff --check PASS. The actual
  current source/config audit reports both disabled options, source verified.

Reference runtime control:
  GCC14 and Clang19 each compile the C fixture -static -O2 -Wall -Wextra -Werror
  in evo-flight-lab:sealed (network none, one CPU/1 GiB). Each probe passes six
  checks: ordinary ROUTE and GENERIC sockets open/close, connector socket fails,
  and errno equals EPROTONOSUPPORT. Combined 12/12 diagnostic checks PASS.
  The SAME flight runs the unchanged original proc_filter: FAIL, exit 1,
  "socket failed: Protocol not supported". Boot and normal shutdown PASS.
  hvf-host; KUnit autorun disabled; installed QEMU drift explicitly recorded.
  These are absence controls, not enabled-connector or new EvoCC acceptance.

An earlier flight emitted plain diagnostic lines rather than TAP. Both probes
returned zero but the runner correctly classified them INVALID_OUTPUT; that
flight remains recorded. Only output framing changed before the final replay,
not its checks or expected values. The original failed in both flights.

The final payload is 4,191,744 bytes, reuses the existing 64 MiB snapshot scratch
disk, and creates no large disk copy. Original executable, config, Image and
scratch hashes were checked before/after; all flights and containers exited.

